WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.567
-Our first guest is
an Oscar winner

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:05.200
starring alongside Nicole Kidman
in the acclaimed film,

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.901
"Being the Ricardos," which is
in theaters and on Prime Video.

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:11.667
Here's Javier Bardem, everyone.

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:13.467
Ah!
That's what I'm talking about!

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:15.067
-Hello, Jimmy.

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:16.400
-That's what I'm talking about,
buddy.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.767
It's so great to see you.

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:19.300
Thank you for -- welcome --
-Good to see you.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.400
-Happy new year.
Thank you for coming on.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.300
I appreciate you doing this.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.634
Maybe a month ago
your lovely wife, Penelope Cruz,

00:00:27.634 --> 00:00:29.901
was on our program
and we talked to her.

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:34.634
And I asked her about --
I've seen video of you on stage

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:38.534
with Bono at a U2 concert
wearing a purple boa.

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:41.234
And I just wanted to hear
your version of the story.

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:42.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:44.601
-My version of the story
is very simple.

00:00:44.601 --> 00:00:48.100
Bono asked us, "Hey, guys,
we are playing in Barcelona

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.100
and we are bringing
like 10 people.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.300
Would you like to get on stage?"

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.300
And I said, "Yes."

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.367
She said, "no,"
at the same time.

00:00:54.367 --> 00:00:57.167
And then I said to Bono, "Bono,
the only thing that I wanted to

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:59.000
tell you is that
if I get on stage,

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.968
some people may not like that.

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:04.701
May go like, 'Hey, what's
that guy doing there?'"

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:06.267
He says, "Okay, do whatever you
have to do."

00:01:06.267 --> 00:01:09.200
So I put a hat on.
I put on a purple boa.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:12.501
I do my most erotic movements
as I could imagine.

00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:13.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:15.501
Because the song was
"Mysterious Ways."

00:01:15.501 --> 00:01:17.934
[ Laughter ]
And then, of course, the song

00:01:17.934 --> 00:01:20.100
finishes and then I took
the hat off

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.834
and the whole stadium was like,
"Boo!"

00:01:22.834 --> 00:01:24.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.901
I said, "I told you, my friend."

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:27.300
-No, no, no.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.467
I actually know people loved it
because it went viral.

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:31.234
Everyone was talking about it.
We actually have a video.

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:33.234
Let's take a look at
Javier Bardem and Bono.

00:01:33.234 --> 00:01:35.300
Look at this.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:39.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.133 --> 00:01:41.400
How awesome is this guy?

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.968
-Look at that.

00:01:43.968 --> 00:01:47.067
-Yeah!
[ Applause ]

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:49.367
People were holding --
That means number one.

00:01:49.367 --> 00:01:50.634
That's the finger you want.

00:01:50.634 --> 00:01:51.968
I saw people were
going like that.

00:01:51.968 --> 00:01:53.567
That's a good thing.

00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:56.033
We also talked about you guys

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:59.200
went to a few parties
at Prince's house.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.934
-Yeah.
-And we love Prince here

00:02:01.934 --> 00:02:04.133
and always love hearing
Prince stories.

00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:06.200
But how do you remember the --

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.267
Do you remember the first party
you went to at his house?

00:02:08.267 --> 00:02:11.033
-Yeah. Well, it was the night
that I won the Oscar.

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:12.167
It was 2008.

00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:15.067
And then I went to his house

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:17.767
because Penelope was
a good friend of him.

00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:21.133
And then I said,
"It's Javier Bardem plus 17."

00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:24.067
Because I brought 17 people
with me to the Oscars.

00:02:24.067 --> 00:02:27.534
Which I don't understand how
in the world today I could fit

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:29.634
17 people in the theater.

00:02:29.634 --> 00:02:32.234
So we went on then.
He was so generous.

00:02:32.234 --> 00:02:35.534
Like, he let all the 17 -- all
the 18 to come to the party.

00:02:35.534 --> 00:02:37.334
-Wow!
-What a sweetheart.

00:02:37.334 --> 00:02:40.567
-But also there's a story
I heard that you're one of

00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:43.367
the reasons why he was late to
one of his concerts.

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:45.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:47.434
-Yeah. That was in London.

00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:49.667
Again, Penelope knew him
very well.

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:51.300
He invited us.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:54.200
Penelope and I and Jordi Molla,
which is a good friend of ours,

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.667
another actor, to have dinner
before the show.

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:59.300
And then we were having dinner
and we took dessert

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.667
and we were having a drink,
two drinks.

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:03.801
And we were like, "Nobody's
coming here to pick us up."

00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:06.968
So I step out of the room and I
said, "Hey, we are here."

00:03:06.968 --> 00:03:08.434
"Ah, are you finished?"
"Yes."

00:03:08.434 --> 00:03:10.501
Then Prince came and said,
"Are you done?"

00:03:10.501 --> 00:03:14.534
"Yes." So he told us
to go to the seats.

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:16.534
We were accompanied
to our seats.

00:03:16.534 --> 00:03:17.901
And then the show started.

00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:19.968
And we were like, "Oh, my God!

00:03:19.968 --> 00:03:24.300
They've been waiting an hour
for us to finish the dinner!"

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:27.367
So that's my Hollywood star
story.

00:03:27.367 --> 00:03:29.167
-Wow!
-I made people wait for an hour.

00:03:29.167 --> 00:03:30.501
-You really are --
-I'm sorry.

00:03:30.501 --> 00:03:32.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.033 --> 00:03:34.234
It's really -- Success has
really gone to your head.

00:03:34.234 --> 00:03:35.567
Oh, my gosh. Yeah.

00:03:35.567 --> 00:03:37.534
That's hilarious that he --

00:03:37.534 --> 00:03:40.067
-I didn't know.
I swear to God, I didn't know.

00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:41.634
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:41.634 --> 00:03:45.934
What happened to me once, I was
at a concert with Billy Joel

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:47.067
at Madison Square Garden.

00:03:47.067 --> 00:03:48.567
I went back to say hi to Billy

00:03:48.567 --> 00:03:50.267
with my mom and dad
before the show.

00:03:50.267 --> 00:03:51.534
And we're talking to Billy,

00:03:51.534 --> 00:03:54.234
and, you know, he's, again,
a super-nice guy.

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:55.868
And we started talking about
doo-wop.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.267
And I go, "Yeah, I love doo-wop.

00:03:57.267 --> 00:03:58.801
My dad used to sing
in the streets."

00:03:58.801 --> 00:04:00.934
And Billy was like, "Oh, yeah?
What'd you sing?"

00:04:00.934 --> 00:04:03.234
We just started singing like
♪ as we stroll ♪

00:04:03.234 --> 00:04:05.100
We just started harmonizing.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:08.200
We must have sang 10 songs.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.567
At least five songs.

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:13.767
And then we're like,
"Dude, it's like 9:00."

00:04:13.767 --> 00:04:15.200
[ Laughter ]
What is going on?

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.334
It's the only time I've think
he's ever been late.

00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:19.734
So again, I'm sorry to everyone
out there.

00:04:19.734 --> 00:04:21.400
That was my fault.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.601
Yeah.
But I did not mean to do that.

00:04:22.601 --> 00:04:24.400
-It's just the passion.
-It's just passion.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:26.000
Yeah, that's all it is.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:28.067
I want to ask you about this
because I've seen

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:30.701
all of your movies and --

00:04:30.701 --> 00:04:32.167
-I'm sorry for you.

00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:34.434
[ Laughter ]
-No, I'm so lucky.

00:04:34.434 --> 00:04:37.267
But a lot of them I would say
are not kid-friendly.

00:04:37.267 --> 00:04:38.634
Most of them.

00:04:38.634 --> 00:04:40.434
But you have kids.

00:04:40.434 --> 00:04:42.067
And I go, "Well, now it's time
to start

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:43.701
doing some things
your kids can see."

00:04:43.701 --> 00:04:45.767
You're in the live remake,

00:04:45.767 --> 00:04:48.267
the live adaptation of
"The Little Mermaid."

00:04:48.267 --> 00:04:51.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Absolutely, yes.

00:04:51.667 --> 00:04:53.868
And here's breaking news.

00:04:53.868 --> 00:04:55.167
I'm playing Ariel.

00:04:55.167 --> 00:04:57.033
[ Laughter ]
-Wow!

00:04:57.033 --> 00:04:58.968
-Where's the cheers?
I don't hear the cheers.

00:04:58.968 --> 00:05:00.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:00.734 --> 00:05:04.033
-Ariel.

00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:07.133
-Don't worry, don't worry.
That's not going to happen.

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:09.901
That will be a horrible
nightmare for the kids.

00:05:09.901 --> 00:05:12.767
But the thing is, once I heard
about the story

00:05:12.767 --> 00:05:15.534
that Rob Marshall,
which is a person that I adore

00:05:15.534 --> 00:05:18.367
and I profoundly deep love
as a person, as a director.

00:05:18.367 --> 00:05:20.501
-Oh, Rob Marshall,
amazing director.

00:05:20.501 --> 00:05:23.267
-When I knew he was going to do
the movie,

00:05:23.267 --> 00:05:25.901
I texted him and said,
"Listen, I'm sure you have

00:05:25.901 --> 00:05:27.934
already casted King Triton,

00:05:27.934 --> 00:05:31.133
but if there is room for
a Triton with an accent,

00:05:31.133 --> 00:05:32.367
I'm here."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.367 --> 00:05:33.701
And he said, "That's funny.

00:05:33.701 --> 00:05:36.300
I'm in the grocery store with
John and we were going to

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:38.334
text you if you were
ever interested."

00:05:38.334 --> 00:05:40.033
It was right in the moment.

00:05:40.033 --> 00:05:43.801
And my, at the time,
6-year-old daughter, I said,

00:05:43.801 --> 00:05:46.067
"I may be in
'The Little Mermaid.'"

00:05:46.067 --> 00:05:47.968
And she was, like,
almost crying.

00:05:47.968 --> 00:05:49.133
[ Audience aws ]

00:05:49.133 --> 00:05:51.567
And I said, "I'm not playing
Ariel, Luna."

00:05:51.567 --> 00:05:53.067
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, exactly, yeah.

00:05:53.067 --> 00:05:54.968
-And she said, "No, you're
playing Triton, right?"

00:05:54.968 --> 00:05:58.868
So yes, and she was so taken by
it that I forgot --

00:05:58.868 --> 00:06:02.167
Of course, that's the best thing
you can do for a movie --

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:04.300
for your daughter.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:06.133
I know you --
You just recently got --

00:06:06.133 --> 00:06:08.133
Your son is a little bit older
than your daughter.

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:09.868
-Yes.
-He's 10.

00:06:09.868 --> 00:06:13.100
And you got to take him to see
a movie with you in it.

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:14.501
You took him to see "Dune."

00:06:14.501 --> 00:06:16.033
-Yes.
-And you're in that.

00:06:16.033 --> 00:06:20.634
To watch your kid watch you,
what -- I mean, that's so --

00:06:20.634 --> 00:06:23.934
-It was the first time
I brought my kid

00:06:23.934 --> 00:06:25.567
to see a movie of mine.

00:06:25.567 --> 00:06:27.734
Thank God the theater
was packed.

00:06:27.734 --> 00:06:31.601
That was before the Omicron hit
so hard everywhere.

00:06:31.601 --> 00:06:34.133
-Yeah.
-So we had popcorn.

00:06:34.133 --> 00:06:35.667
We had a soda.

00:06:35.667 --> 00:06:37.968
And then he was like,
"Dad, you're not in the movie."

00:06:37.968 --> 00:06:39.367
I said, "Hold on, hold on.
Wait, wait.

00:06:39.367 --> 00:06:40.534
It's only at the end."

00:06:40.534 --> 00:06:41.701
-But of course. He's a kid.

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:43.200
-And he loved the movie,
but he's like,

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:45.267
"Where are you, Dad?"
I said, "Shhhh.

00:06:45.267 --> 00:06:47.601
People shouldn't know
that I'm here

00:06:47.601 --> 00:06:49.667
because if they don't like it,
they can scream at me."

00:06:49.667 --> 00:06:52.200
[ Laughter ]
So we were watching the movie

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:55.434
and finally, I show up, and he
kind of -- "Wow."

00:06:55.434 --> 00:06:58.067
Loved it. It was the first time.

00:06:58.067 --> 00:07:01.400
I was so deeply honored
and proud of what I do.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.734
-Proud papa, yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:03.734 --> 00:07:06.100
-"My kid saw it
and he approved it."

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:07.467
-That's a moment right there.

